<article class="env-lemma" id="0240">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0240">Lemma <span data-tag="0240">35.35.3</span>.</a> In the situation of Lemma <a href="/tag/023Y" data-tag="023Y">35.34.6</a> assume that $f : X' \to X$ is surjective and flat. Then the pullback functor is faithful. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $(V_ i, \varphi _ i)$, $i = 1, 2$ be descent data for $X \to S$. Let $\alpha , \beta : V_1 \to V_2$ be morphisms of descent data. Suppose that $f^*\alpha = f^*\beta $. Our task is to show that $\alpha = \beta $. Note that $\alpha $, $\beta $ are morphisms of schemes over $X$, and that $f^*\alpha $, $f^*\beta $ are simply the base changes of $\alpha $, $\beta $ to morphisms over $X'$. Hence the lemma follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/02VX" data-tag="02VX">35.35.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>